\\,$ | $\\, 0.0869 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -1.2 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1075 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1056 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1038 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -1.1 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1271 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1251 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1230 \\,$ |" 13194139535683 false] [17592186059350 1100 "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z \\sim N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z \\geq -1.16).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.04 \\,$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ | $\\, 0.06 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, -1.3 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0901 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0885 \\,$ | $\\, 0.0869 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -1.2 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1075 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1056 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1038 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -1.1 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1271 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1251 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1230 \\,$ |" 13194139535683 true] [17592186059350 1145 "We're given that $Z\\sim N(0,1)$, and we wish to compute\n\n$$\nP(Z \\geq -1.16)\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/265/Source/Images/7d89d5410f6ee87e310a09801bd13918.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$,\n\n$$\nP(Z \\leq z) = \\Phi(z)\n$$\n\nSince the total area under the graph equals $1$, we can express the required probability in terms of $\\Phi(z)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(Z \\ge - 1.16) &= 1 - P(Z < - 1.16) \\\\\n&= 1 - Φ(-1.16)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/265/Source/Images/53dbf3c2f639c2ac352520f9f98d5008.png)\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\n\\Phi(-1.16) = 0.1230\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(Z \\ge - 1.16) &= 1 - Φ(-1.16) \\\\\n&= 1 - 0.1230 \\\\\n&= 0.8770\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535683 false] [17592186059350 1145 "We're given that $Z\\sim N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z \\geq -1.16).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/cac32ab36217820b63574e011488721bf57652fa63b4cbb7e5029fb54ce26243.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z \\leq z) = \\Phi(z).\n$$\n\nSince the total area under the graph equals $1,$ we can express the required probability in terms of $\\Phi(z)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -1.16) & =1-P(Z<-1.16) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-1.16)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/48adcb6bd3b0d12b9bc935b2414d615e0014d905b89a9f7d632306cd30f08580.png)\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\n\\Phi(-1.16) =  0.1230.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -1.16) & =1-Φ(-1.16) \\\\  & =1-0.1230 \\\\  & =0.8770.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535683 true] [17592186059351 1100 "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z \\sim N(0,1)$, compute $P(-0.48 < Z < 1.18)$.\n\n| $z$$\\, 0.07 \\,$$\\, 0.08 \\,$$\\, 0.09 \\,$$\\, -0.5 \\,$ $\\, 0.2843 \\,$ $\\, 0.2810 \\,$ $\\, 0.2776 \\,$ $\\, -0.4 \\,$ $\\, 0.3192 \\,$ $\\, 0.3156 \\,$ $\\, 0.3121 \\,$ $\\, -0.3 \\,$ $\\, 0.3557 \\,$ $\\, 0.3520 \\,$ $\\, 0.3483 \\,$ |  | $z$$\\, 0.07 \\,$$\\, 0.08 \\,$$\\, 0.09 \\,$$\\, 1.0 \\,$ $\\, 0.8577 \\,$ $\\, 0.8599 \\,$ $\\, 0.8621 \\,$ $\\, 1.1 \\,$ $\\, 0.8790 \\,$ $\\, 0.8810 \\,$ $\\, 0.8830 \\,$ $\\, 1.2 \\,$ $\\, 0.8980 \\,$ $\\, 0.8997 \\,$ $\\, 0.9015 \\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |" 13194139535683 false] [17592186059351 1100 "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z \\sim N(0,1),$ compute $P(-0.48 <              Z <              1.18).$\n\n| | $z$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ | $\\, 0.08 \\,$ | $\\, 0.09 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, -0.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.2843 \\,$ | $\\, 0.2810 \\,$ | $\\, 0.2776 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.4 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3192 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3156 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3121 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.3 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3557 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3520 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3483 \\,$ | |  | | $z$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ | $\\, 0.08 \\,$ | $\\, 0.09 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 1.0 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8577 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8599 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8621 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.1 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8790 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8810 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8830 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.2 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8980 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8997 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9015 \\,$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ | $\\, 0.08 \\,$ | $\\, 0.09 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.2843 \\,$ | $\\, 0.2810 \\,$ | $\\, 0.2776 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.4 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3192 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3156 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3121 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.3 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3557 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3520 \\,$ | $\\, 0.3483 \\,$ |\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ | $\\, 0.08 \\,$ | $\\, 0.09 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.0 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8577 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8599 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8621 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.1 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8790 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8810 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8830 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.2 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8980 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8997 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9015 \\,$ |" 13194139535683 true] [17592186059351 1145 "We're given that $Z\\sim N(0,1)$, and we wish to compute $P(-0.48 < Z < 1.18)$. The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/265/Source/Images/871c67fcea91249ce4ac5dd6d527df33.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$,\n\n$$\nP(Z \\leq z) = \\Phi(z)\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $\\Phi(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(-0.48 < Z < 1.18) &= P(Z < 1.18) - P(Z \\le - 0.48) \\\\\n&= P(Z \\le 1.18) - P(Z \\le - 0.48) \\\\\n&= Φ(1.18) - Φ(-0.48)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nΦ(-0.48) &= 0.3156 \\\\\nΦ(1.18) &= 0.8810\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(-0.48 < Z < 1.18) &= Φ(1.18) - Φ(-0.48) \\\\\n&= 0.8810 - 0.3156 \\\\\n&= 0.5654\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535683 false] [17592186059351 1145 "We're given that $Z\\sim N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-0.48 <     Z <   1.18).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/f9011a3355b8261e153842a43be45e9bb07240d88421e37f7297a7d0f807e101.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z \\leq z) = \\Phi(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $\\Phi(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.48<Z<1.18) & =P(Z<1.18)-P(Z\\le -0.48) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 1.18)-P(Z\\le -0.48) \\\\  & =Φ(1.18)-Φ(-0.48)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.48) & =0.3156 \\\\ Φ(1.18) & =0.8810\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.48<Z<1.18) & =Φ(1.18)-Φ(-0.48) \\\\  & =0.8810-0.3156 \\\\  & =0.5654.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535683 true] [17592186059791 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360999 13194139535683 true] [17592186059791 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361006 13194139535683 true] [17592186059791 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361048 13194139535683 true] [17592186059791 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361054 13194139535683 true] [17592186059791 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361061 13194139535683 true] [17592186059792 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361013 13194139535683 true] [17592186059792 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361020 13194139535683 true] [17592186059792 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361027 13194139535683 true] [17592186059792 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361068 13194139535683 true] [17592186059792 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361075 13194139535683 true] [17592186059793 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361034 13194139535683 true] [17592186059793 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361041 13194139535683 true] [17592186059793 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361051 13194139535683 true] [17592186059793 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361082 13194139535683 true] [17592186060369 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535683 true] [17592186060369 1100 "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nThe data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0, 1)$, compute $P(0.70 < Z < 0.92)$.\n\n| $z$ | $0.00$ | $0.01$ | $0.02$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $0.7$ | $0.7580$ | $0.7611$ | $0.7642$ |\n| $0.8$ | $0.7881$ | $0.7910$ | $0.7939$ |\n| $0.9$ | $0.8159$ | $0.8186$ | $0.8212$ |" 13194139535683 false] [17592186060369 1100 "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(0.70<Z<0.92).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7580\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7881\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8159\\,$ | $\\,0.8186\\,$ | $\\,0.8212\\,$ |" 13194139535683 true] [17592186060369 1145 "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(0.70<Z<0.92).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/3eb46852c53e4fa13aaa29c31623153bfef604d138f15c6da67732d5730b785f.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.70<Z<0.92) & =P(Z<0.92)-P(Z\\le 0.70) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.92)-P(Z\\le 0.70) \\\\  & =Φ(0.92)-Φ(0.70)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.70) & =0.7580 \\\\ Φ(0.92) & =0.8212\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.7<Z<0.92) & =Φ(0.92)-Φ(0.70) \\\\  & =0.8212-0.7580 \\\\  & =0.0632.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535683 true] [17592186360999 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361000 13194139535683 true] [17592186360999 1089 "q-131387" 13194139535683 true] [17592186360999 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535683 true] [17592186360